WEBVTT

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.800
"Beyond Hangu Pass"

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.350
Meng Ao, sir! We're pushing the
enemy back both above <i>and </i>below!

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.310
The whole army's morale
has soared sky-high

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.150
with the news of Meng Wu slaying Han Ming!

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.190
Excellent!

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.860
Don't let up, now--keep
fanning those flames!

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.950
At this rate, we can
fend them off entirely!

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:57.950
Sir!

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:58.410
"Qin"

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.120
"Qin"

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.120
Keep going! They're faltering!

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.080
Faster! Take back those stairs!

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.670
We've got momentum here! We can win this!

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:13.000
Hey! Why'd you stop?!

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.380
What is <i>that</i>?

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.590
Eh? What the--

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.520
"Chu"

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.150
En--

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.110
Enemy attack!

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.240
What?!

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.530
It's the Chu army!

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.740
They sneaked up behind us!

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.910
They <i>what</i>?!

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.880
It would seem Wa Lin
really did strike from behind.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:03:00.010
Her elite unit is among the
very best in the entire Chu army.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:03.550
If she's striking the rear
of the Qin army with <i>that</i>,

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.640
five thousand is plenty.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.810
We have Wu Fengming's Wei army

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.690
"Wei"

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.690
standing outside the entrance,
ready to charge in.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:16.570
If someone does manage
to open that gate from within,

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.320
the great Wei army
will burst through at once.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.990
And with that, Hangu Pass,
Qin's national gate, will have fallen.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.080
Those idiots, getting me all panicky.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.790
Despite some shameful
behavior on our part,

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:37.920
it looks like the greatest achievement
will ultimately belong to Chu.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.180
I had my doubts, given
how hard she is to handle,

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:46.430
but bringing Wa Lin
along really paid off in the end.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.350
"Chu"

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:51.850
No!

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:52.810
They're...

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.150
They're looking to help
the Wei troops on the stairs!

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.150
We're done for!

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.320
The Wei soldiers have broken free!

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.280
Hurry--mobilize the reserves
on the opposite side!

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:06.580
Surround Wei <i>and </i>Chu!
Block them off again!

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.160
I-It's no use!

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.000
There are Wei and Chu troops
among our Qin soldiers--

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.040
our commands aren't getting through!

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.830
It's out of control!

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.590
E-Enemies at the gate!

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.300
No! Defend that gate!

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:25.010
Do all you can to
defend it to the very last!

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.100
Hey, uh, boss...

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:32.180
This is bad. <i>Real </i>bad.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:35.150
Scout's report for General Wa Lin!

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:38.360
There's been some loud
cheering beyond Hangu Pass.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.240
It seems our troops have arrived!

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.200
You don't say. So it's over, then.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.000
Fall flat before me!

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.670
That goes for Hangu Pass
<i>and </i>Lord Chunshen <i>and </i>Li Mu!

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:03.630
Let them all prostrate
themselves before Wa Lin!

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.130
All right! That's the way!

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.800
Drag 'em out!

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.820
First one's out!

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.320
What is it? What's going on?

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:24.610
I can't see!

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:28.780
The enemy's at the gate,
dragging the boulders out!

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.540
What's this?

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.920
They're just... one after another...

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.500
Are you kidding me?! What are
our men on the ground even <i>doing</i>?

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.670
It's no good! They're caught up
in a melee with Wei and Chu--

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.510
they can't get near the gate!

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:48.340
And the archers up top
can't shoot straight down!

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.100
All right, the gate itself is in sight!

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.730
We're almost there! Keep draggin'!

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.350
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.900
--Stop that!
--No! Stop!

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.690
Let's open it.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:14.830
So much for the heft of an elder general.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:18.120
Forgive me, my King.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:22.000
My fellow citizens of Qin...

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.880
Hangu Pass...

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.300
No!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.380
...is falling.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:46.360
"Qin"

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.070
"Wang"

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.840
Keep them away from the gate!

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:07.050
We've almost got it open!

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.890
Wang Jian!

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:18.850
Hey! What gives? Hurry up and pull!

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:21.060
There's only two left!

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.650
What's wrong? What are you looking--

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:30.900
We...

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.820
We took it back!

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:36.740
The Wang Jian Army has secured
the entrance and environs!

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.750
The gate is safe!

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.710
Thank... Thank goodness...

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:44.420
Good.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.750
Excellent!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.590
Leave it to Wang Jian!

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:54.340
We did it! Serves 'em right!

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:58.720
Man, they really saved us, eh, boss?

00:07:58.720 --> 00:07:59.890
Yeah--

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.770
and all of Qin with us.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.690
True enough. Still...

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:13.910
What's General Wang Jian
doing here, anyway?

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.460
I have no way of knowing
what's going on beyond the gate,

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:28.380
but that's Qin cheering--
no doubt about it!

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:32.880
It seems that reinforcements
arrived from the right.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.010
That would be Wang Jian, I suppose.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.430
But...

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:42.350
If that's so, what the <i>hell </i>is
his opponent Wu Lu Duo doing?!

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:46.810
"Yan"

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.230
As it happened,

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:54.400
Wu Lu Duo was still in the forts
he had taken from Huan Yi.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.370
He had no choice but to exercise caution.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:05.580
Having lost 8,000 of his best fighters
to Wang Jian's ambush that morning,

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:10.210
Wu Lu Duo kept scouting for Wang Jian's
men hidden in the mountains.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:17.010
A hidden enemy, one even he with his
mountain-tribe powers could not find.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:20.510
Wu Lu Duo shuddered at the thought.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.600
But it made sense
that he couldn't find them.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.020
There never <i>were </i>any troops in hiding.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:29.020
Wang Jian and his ambush troops

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:34.280
had left after the morning battle
to assist at Hangu Pass--

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:40.280
had, in fact, just rescued it
in its hour of crisis.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:42.490
No longer would Wu Lu Duo leave the forts,

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:46.250
bent on attacking
the far side of Hangu Pass.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.670
He had lost a psychological war
against Wang Jian,

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:52.300
who'd anticipated this very move.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:55.050
"Wa"   "Chu"

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.880
"Wa"   "Chu"

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.880
I-Is that...

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.890
The smoke signal for failure?!

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.940
Ba Miu!

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.020
Tch.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.150
--Wa Lin, ma'am--
--Shut up!

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:16.700
B-Begging your pardon!

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.910
It's over.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:22.330
And it's all...

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.700
...<i>Han Ming's </i>fault!

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.580
Wa Lin was right.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.630
The Chu army's defeat in
the wake of Han Ming's death

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:33.420
reverberated throughout
the other battlefields,

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:36.760
putting the coalition army
at a disadvantage.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.720
"Zhao"   "Qin"

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.140
Where'd Zhao's general
Qing She run off to?!

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:47.480
Lord Biao's and Qing She's
armies continued their melee

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:49.730
with no decisive moves on either side.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:54.400
Lord Biao is moving to the right!

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:57.240
He must be coming
after Gongsun Long's army!

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.200
Have Gongsun Long fall back.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:02.820
Give Li Bai five thousand
and have them bolster the right.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:03.990
Sir!

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:05.370
Report!

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:08.370
A message from Li Mu at the coalition HQ!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:13.920
"All Zhao troops,
withdraw to headquarters"!

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:15.590
Wait, <i>what</i>?!

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:17.670
Wh-What could this mean?

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:23.720
Isn't this the day we were
supposed to take Hangu Pass?

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:28.230
Huh?

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:31.850
They're pulling away!

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.650
The tide of battle
has turned in a big way!

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:37.320
On the next battlefield over,
Meng Wu slayed Han Ming,

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:39.780
the commanding general of Chu!

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:41.780
Is that true, He Liao Diao?!

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:44.530
So <i>that's </i>what all that hollerin' was!

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.330
Hot damn!

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:50.830
The Zhao army withdrew due
to the danger of Meng Wu's troops

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:52.830
spilling onto this battlefield.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:58.050
The same can be said
about the other battlefields, too.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.300
Xin...

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:04.760
Things have really
started tilting in our favor!

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.810
They won't recover that easily!

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.560
You're gettin' ahead of yourself.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.890
This war ain't over just yet.

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.060
But at this very moment,

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:20.490
He Liao Diao's prediction was indeed
playing out on the other battlefields.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:25.320
Apart from the Yan army,
the coalition army members

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:29.790
had withdrawn to
their pre-hostilities positions,

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:33.670
indicating that Li Mu's strategy
to launch an attack on the 15th day

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:37.040
had indeed failed.

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:41.340
The Chu army's unthinkable defeat

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:46.220
had twisted every
battlefield beyond repair.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:50.310
Each of the coalition army
generals realized

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:55.440
that conquering Hangu Pass would
now be exceedingly difficult indeed.

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:02.990
"Xianyang"

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:04.780
"Xianyang"

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:04.780
Report!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:07.120
Hangu Pass was on the verge of falling

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:10.450
to the Chu army that had
suddenly appeared beyond it!

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:12.660
--What?!
--The Chu army?!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.920
General Wang Jian appeared
with 10 thousand men

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.460
and annihilated them!

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.630
Wang Jian did?

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:23.050
The gates of Hangu Pass
are sealed tight once more!

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.470
Having lost their means of attack,
and with the tide of battle against them,

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.390
the enemy has withdrawn

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:32.770
to their pre-battle starting positions!

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:33.770
With--

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.350
Withdrawn?!

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.190
Let me make sure I understand:

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:47.570
Do you mean that Hangu Pass
would have fallen

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:51.240
if Wang Jian hadn't shown up?

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:54.330
Exactly right.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:57.420
General Wang Jian has saved us.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:01.630
He's fulfilled his role as shield.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.010
A shield, you say?

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:06.840
The Qin army has been posted into

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:11.720
two clear and separate roles:
offense and defense.

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:16.140
The Meng Wu Army that
destroyed the Chu army is the spear,

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:20.110
while the Wang Jian Army that
saved Hangu Pass is the shield.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:25.820
These two armies hold the key
to the Battle of Hangu Pass.

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:30.030
We had a great deal riding on their might.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:36.040
And for the mysterious Wang Jian
to have done his duty so thoroughly...

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:39.040
Honestly, he surpassed our expectations.

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:43.460
So we bet on both Meng Wu
and Wang Jian--and won.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:47.420
Hmm. And what do we stand to gain from it?

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:50.090
A great deal, one could say.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:54.060
It's clear that the foe was
counting on today's battle.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:15:00.560
That loss and the Chu army's defeat
have created quite the disturbance.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:04.900
The Chu army will be on
the defensive and soon wear out,

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:08.610
while our army has a
steady supply of new recruits,

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.450
including from here in Xianyang.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:15.740
What's more, the coalition army
has the specter of Qi at its back,

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:19.460
so they can't fight an
unnecessarily drawn-out war.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:22.000
We can't let our guard down, of course,

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:27.170
but considering these developments
from their point of view...

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:31.890
it would now be extremely
difficult to conquer Hangu Pass.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.390
Hooray!

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:40.140
Wh-Whoops!

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:41.190
Oh!

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:42.650
Ow, ow, ow...

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:44.900
W-We did it, Xiang!

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:48.400
Qin's soldiers fought so, so hard...

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:49.650
Ow...

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:50.950
Are you okay, Yang?

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.450
Oh, I'm just fine!

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:54.950
The coalition army hasn't left just yet,

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.870
but things are really going in our favor!

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:59.160
Y-Yeah...

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.920
I bet our morale has never been higher--

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:06.380
and all those coalition jerks
must be hanging their heads!

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:09.550
"Jerks," huh?

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:12.930
Still... I'm so glad.

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:16.600
To be honest, I thought we were done for.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:21.190
I mean... just look at how happy I am!

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:25.360
I'm with my beloved Highness,
carrying his child...

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:28.690
I have my dearest Yang by my side...

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:34.490
Like, how can someone
like me be allowed so much joy?

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:39.620
So surely... surely something
terrible must be around the corner.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:41.660
There <i>must </i>be!

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.080
I'm sorry, Yang.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:50.420
In my heart of hearts, I'd given up.

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:51.550
Xiang...

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:54.260
I'm the exact same way.

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:58.140
With what's going on,
there's no one who hasn't lost hope.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:05.770
But they keep on striving
to fight off this awful situation...

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:11.780
The people doing the fighting really
are amazing, aren't they, Xiang?

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:13.070
Uh-huh...

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.880
Long Chuan, doing fine.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.170
Song Zuo, two days of R&R.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:36.760
Chong Yuan can handle his squad.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.180
Hey!

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:40.850
You're fighting again tomorrow, you know!

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.430
What's the big idea,
getting so stinking drunk?!

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:46.810
--Hey, tactician lady!
--Our little Diao has arrived!

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.440
Ugh, dammit!

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:51.940
Wei Ping, Pei Lang,
Tian Yǒu, Tian Yong, Mr. Ze...

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.860
All doing fine. Okay.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:56.200
Workin' hard <i>and </i>workin' late!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.450
C'mon, tactician lady, have a drink!

00:17:58.450 --> 00:17:59.950
Not yet.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:03.080
Got to make sure everyone's all right.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:05.580
But really, don't overdo it.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:09.380
You're looking a little pale.
Better rest a while.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.790
Never mind me.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:14.760
I'm not out there fighting
and bleeding like the rest of you.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:17.260
This? This is nothing.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:20.510
That's... That's our tactician lady!

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:25.730
Why are <i>you </i>drinkin' that?

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:29.230
Well, heck--I guess the
party's already started, huh?

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:33.980
And here I got some of the <i>good </i>stuff,
straight from Lord Biao's army!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:36.780
Cheers!

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:40.030
So how did the war council go?

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:43.200
Nothin' we ain't already heard.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.830
Wang Jian savin' Hangu Pass and all.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:52.920
And with Meng Wu killin' Han Ming,
suddenly we have the upper hand.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.920
What did Lord Biao say?

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:58.130
It's missin' something.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.380
Missing something?

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:00.510
Yeah.

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:04.930
Like, there's gotta be something missin'
if the coalition army's already done.

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:12.770
Something's been botherin' me, too.

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:13.650
Diao...

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.070
What do you think?

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:19.070
Is this the end of the coalition army?

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:28.330
I think it is.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.960
You could think something was missing

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:37.840
since the Zhao army on this battlefield
was fairly lackluster after day one,

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:40.930
while the other sites saw fierce battles.

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:44.010
Today the coalition army
threw everything they had at us--

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:45.560
and failed.

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:49.980
It's hard to imagine them coming up
with another winning strategy now.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.770
Yesss! Well said, Diao!

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:58.190
This war is as good as won!

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.240
Cheers!

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:05.280
But now that you mention it,
something's been bothering <i>me</i>, too.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:11.040
And I bet Xin and I are thinking
of the same thing--the same person.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.830
A person?

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:14.540
Yeah--

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:15.790
<i>him</i>.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:24.850
"Chen, Royal Capital
of the Kingdom of Chu"

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:33.480
First we lose Lord Linwu, then Han Ming...

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:34.150
They wound up holding back
the entirety of our Chu army.

00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:38.320
"King Kaolie of Chu"

00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:38.320
They wound up holding back
the entirety of our Chu army.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:43.280
And now conquering Hangu Pass
will be nearly impossible.

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:48.910
This is nothing but utter
humiliation for the land of Chu!

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:54.250
Slice their disgraced corpses
to ribbons the moment they return!

00:20:55.830 --> 00:21:02.510
Now, does this mean
I was foolish to be stingy?

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:05.220
What say you, Lian Po?

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:08.510
Lian Po, formerly of Zhao's Three Greats,

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:13.230
had defected to Chu
after Qin's Shanyang Offensive.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:16.560
The proud people of Chu

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.530
would have contributed
very little in such a huge war--

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:23.200
even under my command.

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:28.700
If it's stinginess you speak of,
look to General Xiang Yan.

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:33.040
And if I were to mobilize Xiang Yan now,

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:37.330
do you believe he could
rally our army in time?

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:40.210
Impossible.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:42.010
What?

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:47.050
Qin has soldiers stationed
at all their castle towns--

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:49.970
not sent to join the Hangu Pass fray,

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:53.980
but instead focused
on defending their posts.

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:56.560
A clever way to fight.

00:21:56.560 --> 00:22:00.440
They'll have patched the holes
made by the invading armies.

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:03.740
Sending reinforcements to Hangu Pass now

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:08.030
would mean fighting
past them all over again.

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:14.250
But <i>I'm </i>saying that unless we <i>do</i>,
Chu will be the villain in this war!

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:22.130
This war is yet to be definitively lost.

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:25.800
You're all missing something crucial:

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:31.680
Who is the biggest nuisance
in this coalition army?

00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:37.390
The most dangerous man
in the entire Middle Kingdom?

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:39.100
Who is it?

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:42.270
Li Mu, of course!

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:44.400
Li Mu, still one of the Three Greats,

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:47.990
who buried Wang Yi,
the last of the Six Great Generals,

00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:51.280
three years ago at Mǎyáng!

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:58.790
Why, he's yet to make
a single move in this battle.

00:22:58.790 --> 00:23:00.630
There's no doubt

00:23:00.630 --> 00:23:04.090
he's got something up his sleeve again.

00:23:07.470 --> 00:23:13.600
Very few in the coalition army,
much less the Qin army,

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:19.060
knew that Li Mu disappeared
from the coalition army that night.

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:58.580
Next on <i>Kingdom</i>: "Li Mu's Whereabouts."
